+ * LINUX64 (xnulinux): an exception taken on an XNU kernel stack enters Linux's vectors, whose overflow check wants
+ * bit THREAD_SHIFT (14) of sp clear, as on Linux's 2*THREAD_SIZE-aligned stacks. Hosted, each stack starts on a
+ * 32 KiB boundary: the allocation is 32 KiB aligned and the stack sits 32 KiB above its start (guard pages first,
+ * then unused wired pages, then the stack, then the upper guard page).
